# {{ .APP_NAME }}

Node.js + TypeScript Voice Agent host. Opens a WebSocket session, prints
the agent's transcripts to stdout, and registers a stub
`getCurrentWeather` tool the agent can invoke.

## Prerequisites

- Node 20+
- A running SpeechKit Server with Voice Agent enabled
- (optional) Bearer token for `auth_mode = "bearer"` deployments

## Configure

```sh
cp .env.example .env
# edit .env to point at your SpeechKit deployment
```

## Run

```sh
npm install
npm run dev
```

Then type sentences in the terminal to inject user-turns. Type
`/quit` to close the session cleanly.

## Adding tools

Edit [src/tools.ts](src/tools.ts) to add new tools. Each tool exposes a
JSON-Schema describing its parameters and an `invoke(args)` function.
The included `getCurrentWeather` tool is a deterministic stub — replace
its `invoke` with a real provider call.

For Voice Agent persona/role configuration that registers tools at
session-start, see <https://speechkit.cc/api/openapi.v1.yaml> under
`POST /v1/personas`.

## Frame protocol

The full WebSocket protocol is documented in
<https://speechkit.cc/api/asyncapi.v1.yaml>. This template implements
the handler subset needed for text-only conversations + tool dispatch:
`start`, `text`, `tool_response`, `stop` (out) and `state`,
`input_transcript`, `output_transcript`, `tool_call`, `error`,
`session_end` (in). Binary audio frames are received but skipped.
